// TEST: Physics -- Fishing for q: Time-Ordered Crossings in a Classical Cascade
// ============================================================================
// The q-deformation question, cast at the DYNAMICS. In free probability the
// fourth mixed moment of a family weights pair partitions by q^(#crossings):
//   E[x_i x_j x_k x_l] = c_ij c_kl + q * c_ik c_jl + c_il c_jk   (i<j<k<l),
// q = 1 classical (Wick), q = 0 free (non-crossing only). For TIME-ordered
// observables the crossing pairing (ik)(jl) is the interleaved -- "out of
// time order" -- contraction. Question: does a classical fuzzy cascade
// suppress (q < 1) or enhance (q > 1) its crossing channel, and is the
// deformation a CONSTANT (a bona fide q) across quadruples?
// Setup, entirely in Blade (no external data): a 7-ball Newton's-cradle
// cascade, projectile m0 = 1 sharp at u = 1; six target masses carry 3-point
// jets with ALTERNATING wide/tight widths (heterogeneity breaks the
// exponential-kernel degeneracy c_ik c_jl = c_il c_jk that would make the
// crossing channel unidentifiable). Ensemble = the full 3^6 = 729 product
// grid, built in-language from range + floor digits. Observables: the
// transmitted front velocities X_1..X_6 (closed-form chain, exact per
// realization; the front outruns every follower -- guarded below -- so no
// event loop and no order ambiguity: this cascade's itinerary is sharp by
// design, isolating the CUMULANT structure from the order gauge of 21-26).
// For each of the 15 time-ordered quadruples: connected 4-cumulant kappa4,
// then the deformation read through each pairing channel,
//   g = kappa4 / (channel product),  q_hat = 1 + kappa4 / (c_ik c_jl).
// FINDINGS (pinned below):
//   * ALL FIFTEEN CONNECTED 4-CUMULANTS ARE NEGATIVE -- a uniform deficit
//     below the Wick sum -- but it is NOT crossing suppression. Attributed
//     to the crossing channel, the would-be deformation ranges over
//     q_hat = -0.37 .. +5.50 with sign changes (rsd of the deformation
//     constant = 1.23): NOT_A_Q_FAMILY. The sign changes come from
//     near-null, ANTICORRELATED covariance channels (consecutive collisions
//     share a mass, and its two roles -- receiving slow, passing fast --
//     partially cancel): the would-be normalizer itself dies.
//   * BELOW FREE: on the well-conditioned quadruples 2/5 land at q_hat < 0
//     -- the deficit EXCEEDS the entire crossing product, so no q in [0,1]
//     (the whole classical-to-free interpolation) can produce it. The
//     structure is not a partition-channel deformation at all.
//   * THE CONTROL NAILS THE MECHANISM. Reweight the SAME grid, SAME
//     dynamics from uniform (digit kurtosis -2/3, platykurtic) to
//     leptokurtic jets (p = 1/12, kurtosis +1/12): ALL 15 kappa4 flip
//     positive (15/15). Kurtosis in, kurtosis out: the cascade TRANSPORTS
//     the jet's fourth cumulant. Verdict: INHERITED_NOT_DYNAMICAL.
//   * THE CHANNELS NEVER SEPARATE. Cross/nested normalizer ratios sit at
//     0.97..1.03: a multiplicative cascade's covariance nearly factorizes,
//     so "which pairing channel" is dynamically ill-posed here -- the
//     deformation statistics are channel-blind (rsd 1.233 vs 1.225).
//   * Verdict for the arc: classical few-body fuzz carries NO q. Where a
//     genuine, universal q-deformation does live is the OBSERVER's own
//     spectral noise -- example 30.
// Quantum contrast: in quantum chaos, crossing-suppressed multi-time
// correlators (the free-probability structure of ETH, OTOC decay) are a
// hallmark of the DYNAMICS itself. Classically, mixing without phases
// transports the input tower's shape but cannot reshape the partition
// lattice: dynamical crossing suppression is a genuinely quantum signature.
// ============================================================================
import ppl as ppl

// --- the 3^6 product grid from digits (uniform 3-point jets per mass):
//     realization r's six base-3 digits, lifted over the range 0..729 ---
let R = Float64(0..729)
let D1 = R - 3.0 * floor(R / 3.0)
let D2 = floor(R / 3.0) - 3.0 * floor(R / 9.0)
let D3 = floor(R / 9.0) - 3.0 * floor(R / 27.0)
let D4 = floor(R / 27.0) - 3.0 * floor(R / 81.0)
let D5 = floor(R / 81.0) - 3.0 * floor(R / 243.0)
let D6 = floor(R / 243.0) - 3.0 * floor(R / 729.0)

// --- masses: centers ~1, ALTERNATING wide/tight jets (all within [0.85,1.15]) ---
let M1 = 1.05 + 0.10 * (D1 - 1.0)
let M2 = 0.94 + 0.025 * (D2 - 1.0)
let M3 = 1.07 + 0.08 * (D3 - 1.0)
let M4 = 0.96 + 0.03 * (D4 - 1.0)
let M5 = 1.04 + 0.11 * (D5 - 1.0)
let M6 = 0.93 + 0.02 * (D6 - 1.0)

// --- transmitted-front chain: X_k = X_{k-1} * 2 m_{k-1} / (m_{k-1} + m_k) ---
let X1 = 2.0 / (1.0 + M1)
let X2 = X1 * 2.0 * M1 / (M1 + M2)
let X3 = X2 * 2.0 * M2 / (M2 + M3)
let X4 = X3 * 2.0 * M3 / (M3 + M4)
let X5 = X4 * 2.0 * M4 / (M4 + M5)
let X6 = X5 * 2.0 * M5 / (M5 + M6)

// --- followers F_k = X_{k-1} (m_{k-1} - m_k)/(m_{k-1} + m_k); guard: the
//     front outruns every follower in every realization (X_k exact) ---
let F1 = (1.0 - M1) / (1.0 + M1)
let F2 = X1 * (M1 - M2) / (M1 + M2)
let F3 = X2 * (M2 - M3) / (M2 + M3)
let F4 = X3 * (M3 - M4) / (M3 + M4)
let F5 = X4 * (M4 - M5) / (M4 + M5)
let F6 = X5 * (M5 - M6) / (M5 + M6)
let W2 = method_for(zip(F1, F2)) <@> lambda(a, b) -> (if abs(a) > abs(b) then abs(a) else abs(b)) |> compute
// running max of |F_k|: the same kernel folds each further follower in
let widen = lambda(a, b) -> (if a > abs(b) then a else abs(b))
let W3 = method_for(zip(W2, F3)) <@> widen |> compute
let W4 = method_for(zip(W3, F4)) <@> widen |> compute
let W5 = method_for(zip(W4, F5)) <@> widen |> compute
let W6 = method_for(zip(W5, F6)) <@> widen |> compute
let GUARD = reduce(method_for(zip(W6, X6)) <@> lambda(w, x) -> (if w < x then 0.0 else 1.0), (+))
let guard_V = if GUARD < 0.5 then "FRONT_OUTRUNS_ALL" else "ITINERARY_AT_RISK"

// --- centered columns ---
// the six transmitted fronts are six variables over one 729-realization
// sample axis -- the multivariate object the whole 4-cumulant analysis is
// about -- so their first-order block is a single former read.
let XALL: Array<Float64 like Idx<6>, Idx<729>> = [X1, X2, X3, X4, X5, X6]
let x_m1 = ppl.moments(XALL, 1)
let mu1 = x_m1(0)
let mu2 = x_m1(1)
let mu3 = x_m1(2)
let mu4 = x_m1(3)
let mu5 = x_m1(4)
let mu6 = x_m1(5)
let Y1 = X1 - mu1
let Y2 = X2 - mu2
let Y3 = X3 - mu3
let Y4 = X4 - mu4
let Y5 = X5 - mu5
let Y6 = X6 - mu6

// --- the 15 pair covariances (exact ensemble sums) ---
let c12 = prodsum(Y1, Y2) / 729.0
let c13 = prodsum(Y1, Y3) / 729.0
let c14 = prodsum(Y1, Y4) / 729.0
let c15 = prodsum(Y1, Y5) / 729.0
let c16 = prodsum(Y1, Y6) / 729.0
let c23 = prodsum(Y2, Y3) / 729.0
let c24 = prodsum(Y2, Y4) / 729.0
let c25 = prodsum(Y2, Y5) / 729.0
let c26 = prodsum(Y2, Y6) / 729.0
let c34 = prodsum(Y3, Y4) / 729.0
let c35 = prodsum(Y3, Y5) / 729.0
let c36 = prodsum(Y3, Y6) / 729.0
let c45 = prodsum(Y4, Y5) / 729.0
let c46 = prodsum(Y4, Y6) / 729.0
let c56 = prodsum(Y5, Y6) / 729.0

// --- central 4-point moments for the 15 time-ordered quadruples ---
let p1234 = reduce(Y1 * Y2 * Y3 * Y4, (+)) / 729.0
let p1235 = reduce(Y1 * Y2 * Y3 * Y5, (+)) / 729.0
let p1236 = reduce(Y1 * Y2 * Y3 * Y6, (+)) / 729.0
let p1245 = reduce(Y1 * Y2 * Y4 * Y5, (+)) / 729.0
let p1246 = reduce(Y1 * Y2 * Y4 * Y6, (+)) / 729.0
let p1256 = reduce(Y1 * Y2 * Y5 * Y6, (+)) / 729.0
let p1345 = reduce(Y1 * Y3 * Y4 * Y5, (+)) / 729.0
let p1346 = reduce(Y1 * Y3 * Y4 * Y6, (+)) / 729.0
let p1356 = reduce(Y1 * Y3 * Y5 * Y6, (+)) / 729.0
let p1456 = reduce(Y1 * Y4 * Y5 * Y6, (+)) / 729.0
let p2345 = reduce(Y2 * Y3 * Y4 * Y5, (+)) / 729.0
let p2346 = reduce(Y2 * Y3 * Y4 * Y6, (+)) / 729.0
let p2356 = reduce(Y2 * Y3 * Y5 * Y6, (+)) / 729.0
let p2456 = reduce(Y2 * Y4 * Y5 * Y6, (+)) / 729.0
let p3456 = reduce(Y3 * Y4 * Y5 * Y6, (+)) / 729.0

// --- connected 4-cumulants: kappa4 = p - seq - cross - nest ---
let k1234 = p1234 - c12 * c34 - c13 * c24 - c14 * c23
let k1235 = p1235 - c12 * c35 - c13 * c25 - c15 * c23
let k1236 = p1236 - c12 * c36 - c13 * c26 - c16 * c23
let k1245 = p1245 - c12 * c45 - c14 * c25 - c15 * c24
let k1246 = p1246 - c12 * c46 - c14 * c26 - c16 * c24
let k1256 = p1256 - c12 * c56 - c15 * c26 - c16 * c25
let k1345 = p1345 - c13 * c45 - c14 * c35 - c15 * c34
let k1346 = p1346 - c13 * c46 - c14 * c36 - c16 * c34
let k1356 = p1356 - c13 * c56 - c15 * c36 - c16 * c35
let k1456 = p1456 - c14 * c56 - c15 * c46 - c16 * c45
let k2345 = p2345 - c23 * c45 - c24 * c35 - c25 * c34
let k2346 = p2346 - c23 * c46 - c24 * c36 - c26 * c34
let k2356 = p2356 - c23 * c56 - c25 * c36 - c26 * c35
let k2456 = p2456 - c24 * c56 - c25 * c46 - c26 * c45
let k3456 = p3456 - c34 * c56 - c35 * c46 - c36 * c45

// --- deformation constants per channel: g = kappa4 / (channel product) ---
// crossing channel (ik)(jl): the interleaved, "out-of-time-order" pairing
let g1234 = k1234 / (c13 * c24)
let g1235 = k1235 / (c13 * c25)
let g1236 = k1236 / (c13 * c26)
let g1245 = k1245 / (c14 * c25)
let g1246 = k1246 / (c14 * c26)
let g1256 = k1256 / (c15 * c26)
let g1345 = k1345 / (c14 * c35)
let g1346 = k1346 / (c14 * c36)
let g1356 = k1356 / (c15 * c36)
let g1456 = k1456 / (c15 * c46)
let g2345 = k2345 / (c24 * c35)
let g2346 = k2346 / (c24 * c36)
let g2356 = k2356 / (c25 * c36)
let g2456 = k2456 / (c25 * c46)
let g3456 = k3456 / (c35 * c46)
// nested channel (il)(jk), for the collapse comparison
let h1234 = k1234 / (c14 * c23)
let h1235 = k1235 / (c15 * c23)
let h1236 = k1236 / (c16 * c23)
let h1245 = k1245 / (c15 * c24)
let h1246 = k1246 / (c16 * c24)
let h1256 = k1256 / (c16 * c25)
let h1345 = k1345 / (c15 * c34)
let h1346 = k1346 / (c16 * c34)
let h1356 = k1356 / (c16 * c35)
let h1456 = k1456 / (c16 * c45)
let h2345 = k2345 / (c25 * c34)
let h2346 = k2346 / (c26 * c34)
let h2356 = k2356 / (c26 * c35)
let h2456 = k2456 / (c26 * c45)
let h3456 = k3456 / (c36 * c45)

// --- collapse statistics: is there ONE q? which channel collapses tighter? ---
// the fifteen per-quadruple values as arrays (time-ordered, lexicographic):
// every statistic below is a fold over them
let G = [g1234, g1235, g1236, g1245, g1246, g1256, g1345, g1346, g1356, g1456, g2345, g2346, g2356, g2456, g3456]
let H = [h1234, h1235, h1236, h1245, h1246, h1256, h1345, h1346, h1356, h1456, h2345, h2346, h2356, h2456, h3456]
let K4 = [k1234, k1235, k1236, k1245, k1246, k1256, k1345, k1346, k1356, k1456, k2345, k2346, k2356, k2456, k3456]
let gbar = reduce(G, (+)) / 15.0
let gvar = reduce((G - gbar) * (G - gbar), (+)) / 15.0
let g_rsd = sqrt(gvar) / abs(gbar)
let hbar = reduce(H, (+)) / 15.0
let hvar = reduce((H - hbar) * (H - hbar), (+)) / 15.0
let h_rsd = sqrt(hvar) / abs(hbar)

// --- sign census and extremes of q_hat = 1 + g ---
let npos = reduce(method_for(K4) <@> lambda(k) -> (if k > 0.0 then 1.0 else 0.0), (+))
let g_min = reduce(G, lambda(a, b) -> if a < b then a else b)
let g_max = reduce(G, lambda(a, b) -> if a > b then a else b)
let qhat_min = 1.0 + g_min
let qhat_max = 1.0 + g_max

// --- degeneracy meter: the design must separate cross from nested products ---
let r1234 = (c13 * c24) / (c14 * c23)
let r1256 = (c15 * c26) / (c16 * c25)
let r1345 = (c14 * c35) / (c15 * c34)
let r2456 = (c25 * c46) / (c26 * c45)
let r3456 = (c35 * c46) / (c36 * c45)

// --- clean-family statistics (quadruples avoiding the near-null ball-2 channels) ---
let GC = [g1345, g1346, g1356, g1456, g3456]
let gcbar = reduce(GC, (+)) / 5.0
let gcvar = reduce((GC - gcbar) * (GC - gcbar), (+)) / 5.0
let gc_rsd = sqrt(gcvar) / abs(gcbar)
let n_below_free = reduce(method_for(GC) <@> lambda(g) -> (if g < -1.0 then 1.0 else 0.0), (+))

// --- THE CONTROL: same grid, same dynamics, LEPTOKURTIC jet weights.
//     Reweight each digit (p, 1-2p, p) with p = 1/12: per-digit kurtosis
//     flips from -2/3 (uniform, platykurtic) to +1/12 (leptokurtic).
//     If the kappa4 tower flips sign wholesale, the 4-cumulant structure is
//     INPUT-INHERITED -- transported jet shape -- not dynamical deformation. ---
let lepto = lambda(d) -> (if d > 0.5 then (if d < 1.5 then 2.5 else 0.25) else 0.25)
let U1 = method_for(D1) <@> lepto |> compute
let U2 = method_for(D2) <@> lepto |> compute
let U3 = method_for(D3) <@> lepto |> compute
let U4 = method_for(D4) <@> lepto |> compute
let U5 = method_for(D5) <@> lepto |> compute
let U6 = method_for(D6) <@> lepto |> compute
let WA = U1 * U2 * U3
let WB = U4 * U5 * U6
let WT = WA * WB
let wsum = reduce(WT, (+))

let mw1 = prodsum(WT, X1) / 729.0
let mw2 = prodsum(WT, X2) / 729.0
let mw3 = prodsum(WT, X3) / 729.0
let mw4 = prodsum(WT, X4) / 729.0
let mw5 = prodsum(WT, X5) / 729.0
let mw6 = prodsum(WT, X6) / 729.0
let Z1 = X1 - mw1
let Z2 = X2 - mw2
let Z3 = X3 - mw3
let Z4 = X4 - mw4
let Z5 = X5 - mw5
let Z6 = X6 - mw6

let w12 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z2, (+)) / 729.0
let w13 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z3, (+)) / 729.0
let w14 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z4, (+)) / 729.0
let w15 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z5, (+)) / 729.0
let w16 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let w23 = reduce(WT * Z2 * Z3, (+)) / 729.0
let w24 = reduce(WT * Z2 * Z4, (+)) / 729.0
let w25 = reduce(WT * Z2 * Z5, (+)) / 729.0
let w26 = reduce(WT * Z2 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let w34 = reduce(WT * Z3 * Z4, (+)) / 729.0
let w35 = reduce(WT * Z3 * Z5, (+)) / 729.0
let w36 = reduce(WT * Z3 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let w45 = reduce(WT * Z4 * Z5, (+)) / 729.0
let w46 = reduce(WT * Z4 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let w56 = reduce(WT * Z5 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0

let s1234 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z2 * Z3 * Z4, (+)) / 729.0
let s1235 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z2 * Z3 * Z5, (+)) / 729.0
let s1236 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z2 * Z3 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let s1245 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z2 * Z4 * Z5, (+)) / 729.0
let s1246 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z2 * Z4 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let s1256 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z2 * Z5 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let s1345 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z3 * Z4 * Z5, (+)) / 729.0
let s1346 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z3 * Z4 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let s1356 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z3 * Z5 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let s1456 = reduce(WT * Z1 * Z4 * Z5 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let s2345 = reduce(WT * Z2 * Z3 * Z4 * Z5, (+)) / 729.0
let s2346 = reduce(WT * Z2 * Z3 * Z4 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let s2356 = reduce(WT * Z2 * Z3 * Z5 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let s2456 = reduce(WT * Z2 * Z4 * Z5 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0
let s3456 = reduce(WT * Z3 * Z4 * Z5 * Z6, (+)) / 729.0

let kw1234 = s1234 - w12 * w34 - w13 * w24 - w14 * w23
let kw1235 = s1235 - w12 * w35 - w13 * w25 - w15 * w23
let kw1236 = s1236 - w12 * w36 - w13 * w26 - w16 * w23
let kw1245 = s1245 - w12 * w45 - w14 * w25 - w15 * w24
let kw1246 = s1246 - w12 * w46 - w14 * w26 - w16 * w24
let kw1256 = s1256 - w12 * w56 - w15 * w26 - w16 * w25
let kw1345 = s1345 - w13 * w45 - w14 * w35 - w15 * w34
let kw1346 = s1346 - w13 * w46 - w14 * w36 - w16 * w34
let kw1356 = s1356 - w13 * w56 - w15 * w36 - w16 * w35
let kw1456 = s1456 - w14 * w56 - w15 * w46 - w16 * w45
let kw2345 = s2345 - w23 * w45 - w24 * w35 - w25 * w34
let kw2346 = s2346 - w23 * w46 - w24 * w36 - w26 * w34
let kw2356 = s2356 - w23 * w56 - w25 * w36 - w26 * w35
let kw2456 = s2456 - w24 * w56 - w25 * w46 - w26 * w45
let kw3456 = s3456 - w34 * w56 - w35 * w46 - w36 * w45
let KW = [kw1234, kw1235, kw1236, kw1245, kw1246, kw1256, kw1345, kw1346, kw1356, kw1456, kw2345, kw2346, kw2356, kw2456, kw3456]
let nposW = reduce(method_for(KW) <@> lambda(k) -> (if k > 0.0 then 1.0 else 0.0), (+))

// --- verdicts ---
let sign_V = if npos < 0.5 then "ALL_K4_NEGATIVE" else (if npos > 14.5 then "ALL_K4_POSITIVE" else "MIXED_SIGNS")
let collapse_V = if g_rsd < 0.25 then "CONSTANT_Q" else "NOT_A_Q_FAMILY"
let below_V = if n_below_free > 0.5 then "DEFICIT_EXCEEDS_CROSSING_CHANNEL" else "WITHIN_Q_RANGE"
let flip_V = if nposW > 14.5 then "K4_FLIPS_WITH_JET_SHAPE" else (if nposW < 0.5 then "K4_SIGN_ROBUST" else "PARTIAL_FLIP")
let verdict_V = if nposW > 14.5 then "INHERITED_NOT_DYNAMICAL" else "DYNAMICAL_STRUCTURE"

// itinerary sharp; all fifteen 4-cumulants negative yet no q fits (sign-
// changing, below-free); the leptokurtic reweighting flips all fifteen:
// the cascade transports jet kurtosis, it does not deform partitions:
// EXPECT: GUARD = 0.0
// EXPECT: guard_V = "FRONT_OUTRUNS_ALL"
// EXPECT: mu1 = 0.977161113292714
// EXPECT: c24 = -3.5012903526175e-06
// EXPECT: c34 = 0.000123559375534494
// EXPECT: c56 = 0.000200177543354424
// EXPECT: k1345 = -1.1075006147166e-09
// EXPECT: k3456 = -1.77047640617364e-09
// EXPECT: npos = 0.0
// EXPECT: g1345 = -0.0815388688880832
// EXPECT: g1456 = -1.14327540947602
// EXPECT: g3456 = -1.36880649543928
// EXPECT: g_rsd = 1.23287864289238
// EXPECT: h_rsd = 1.22536115263124
// EXPECT: qhat_min = -0.36880649543928
// EXPECT: qhat_max = 5.49678099037086
// EXPECT: r1234 = 1.03018858959444
// EXPECT: r3456 = 0.974555461264268
// EXPECT: gcbar = -0.552949835052889
// EXPECT: gc_rsd = 1.04619278954239
// EXPECT: n_below_free = 2.0
// EXPECT: wsum = 729.0
// EXPECT: kw1345 = 3.62563580758112e-10
// EXPECT: kw3456 = 3.75291383123026e-10
// EXPECT: nposW = 15.0
// EXPECT: sign_V = "ALL_K4_NEGATIVE"
// EXPECT: collapse_V = "NOT_A_Q_FAMILY"
// EXPECT: below_V = "DEFICIT_EXCEEDS_CROSSING_CHANNEL"
// EXPECT: flip_V = "K4_FLIPS_WITH_JET_SHAPE"
// EXPECT: verdict_V = "INHERITED_NOT_DYNAMICAL"
